{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/706475-looking-for-a-group-in-vancouver-bc","id":706475,"title":"Looking for a group in Vancouver, BC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-18T01:26:54-07:00","id":706475,"title":"Looking for a group in Vancouver, BC","content":"My wife and I moved from Serbia to Canada a bit over a month ago. We've just gotten kinda-sorta settled in and, of course, the first thing that comes to mind is that now we really need a new local game group. Not that surprising for a family that switches continents carrying with them nothing but clothes and 200 RPG books... So, yeah. I have my priorities <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We're most interested in nWoD of any kind and, since Ex3 is now really just around the bend, that's of great interest as well. Eclipse Phase and Mindjammer also come to mind as games of interest. Though, really, we'd pretty much be up for any game that isn't D&amp;D or Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> A bit about us - we're 34 and 33, speak English pretty well and currently reside in Vancouver. More specifically, Kitsilano. We wouldn't mind traveling pretty much anywhere in the city for a game and our place is certainly open for hosting game sessions. I have a lot of experience running games but for the time being I'd prefer to have someone else ST as things are pretty hectic right now and I just don't think I could do as good a job under the circumstances as I'd like.<br /> <br /> Didn't get the impression that a lot of Vancouverites reside on these forums but I figured it's worth a shot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edi